  "question": {
    "text": "A sand dropper drops sand of mass $m(t)$ on a conveyer belt at a rate proportional to the square root of speed $(v)$ of the belt, i.e. $\\frac{\\mathrm{dm}}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\propto \\sqrt{v}$. If P is the power delivered to run the belt at constant speed then which of the following relationship is true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QZvDh",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\propto \\sqrt{v}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nA9tH",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\propto v$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZJbor",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}^2 \\propto v^5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "KTaq1",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}^2 \\propto v^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Power $=\\vec{F} \\cdot \\vec{V}$\nand $F=\\frac{d p}{d t}=$ Rate of change of linear momentum\n$F=V \\cdot \\frac{d m}{d t}=K_1 V^{\\frac{3}{2}}, K$ is constant\nPower $(P)=\\left(K V^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right) \\cdot(V)$\n$=K V^{\\frac{5}{2}}$\n\nSo, $P^2 \\propto V^5$",
    "image": null
  },
